WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.542 --> 00:00:02.210
You really care about them, don't you?

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.505
I think they're a bunch of
absolute losers.

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.215
But they're my losers.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.815
This is the pre-boarding announcement

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:28.403
for Lusit Airways flight LLT154
to Marrakech.

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:31.030
We are now inviting
those classified as small children…

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:32.323
Come on. Where are you?

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:40.248
Please have your boarding pass
and identification ready. Thank you.

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:42.709
-ETA?
-Less than a minute.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:55.597
-Has there been a handover?
-Negative.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:01.728
Eyes on Dogs.

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:13.072
Why is he airside?
Intel said target was inbound.

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:14.616
He made visual contact, ma'am.

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:15.825
Reconfirm.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.660
Second Desk requests we reconfirm visual.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:21.414
You're looking for an Asian male,
20s, backpack, blue shirt, white tee.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.793
Yes, confirmed,
and I have Dogs on standing by.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:31.549
Shit.

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.760
Lost visual. Possible handover.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:35.345
What does he mean "possible handover"?

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.555
-Cartwright, clarify.
-Did you catch anything on CCTV?

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:41.893
Negative, that's what you're there for.
Repeat, clarify.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:43.603
He has a visual.
Did he see a handover or not?

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.563
Lost visual momentarily.

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:47.440
Repeat, possible handover.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:50.109
-Come on. Get out of the way.
-Blocked by the cleaner.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.112
Lusit Airways are pleased
to announce boarding

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:56.157
for flight LLT154 to Marrakech.

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:59.410
We would like to invite families
and those requiring assistance

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:01.246
-to come forward first.
-Move, move, move.

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.957
Please have your passports
and boarding card ready.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.460
Okay, have full visual on target again,

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.712
but something has definitely gone
in or out of that backpack.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.797
Tell him to hold.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.216
Cartwright, hold your position.
Do not intercept.

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:17.804
-Target is on the move.
-We have eyes on target. Hold.

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:18.888
Ma'am?

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:23.518
Hold your position, Cartwright.
Hold your position. We are assessing.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.812
Target is joining the queue to board.
Standing by.

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:27.313
Keep the channel clear, please.

00:02:29.065 --> 00:02:30.191
Come on.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.027
Second Desk says,
"Do not intercept."

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:37.740
Come on, come on, come on, come on.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.538
-Push the button.
-Dogs are standing by, ma'am.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.293
At least he's heading downstairs.
There's 300 bodies up there.

00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:50.587
Yes, but he's headed to
a plane loaded with fuel.

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.673
First passengers are
on the tarmac, ma'am.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.513
-Authorize.
-Apprehend suspect.

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:01.681
Dogs, go.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.892
Move!

00:03:07.562 --> 00:03:09.689
-Out of the way!
-Move!

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:13.276
-Down, down, down!
-What the fuck?

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.652
Get the fuck off me!

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:18.072
Disperse if you can. Keep calm.

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:20.450
-Get back!
-Get off me!

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.201
-What the fuck?
-Relax!

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:23.870
-What are you doing?
-No trigger.

00:03:23.953 --> 00:03:25.622
-This is fucking harassment!
-No wires here.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.415
-Clear.
-Bag.

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:30.668
-Get off! Get off me.
-Over.

00:03:33.838 --> 00:03:37.342
Somebody film this! Fuck!

00:03:37.425 --> 00:03:39.677
-Get off me! Nothing on me!
-Stop moving!

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:45.350
He's clean.

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:48.019
Repeat. Repeat!

00:03:48.102 --> 00:03:50.521
He's clean.
There's no device, no weapon. Nothing.

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:52.148
-Ma'am?
-He has the wrong suspect,

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.317
or we have the wrong intel,
and we don't have the wrong intel.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.694
-Ma'am, he reconfirmed visual.
-Reconfirm again.

00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:58.529
Cartwright, confirm suspect description.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:02.241
Asian male, 20s, backpack,
blue shirt, white tee.

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:03.826
I said, "white shirt, blue tee."

00:04:05.119 --> 00:04:06.245
You--

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:09.457
No, no, no, no, you said--
you said, "blue shirt, white tee."

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.084
Webb.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.168
Yeah.

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:15.088
Shit. Put it on the main screen.

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:17.507
White shirt, blue tee. Suspect is inbound.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.634
Inbound, headed to immigration,
main terminal.

00:04:19.717 --> 00:04:21.052
Stand Cartwright down. He's done.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:23.429
Second Desk says
stand down, Cartwright.

00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:27.350
Oh, shit.

00:04:28.726 --> 00:04:30.687
-Stand him down.
-Cartwright, where are you going?

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.563
You tailed the wrong suspect.
You're stood down.

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:34.399
Get me CCTV on that escalator now.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:41.572
-Should we have immigration hold him up?
-Not with a bomb on his back.

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:43.199
-Get SO15 on standby.
-Ma'am.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.951
SO15, standby.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.750
-He'll be through in two minutes.
-Duffy, where are your Dogs?

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.252
Still airside with Cartwright's suspect.

00:04:54.335 --> 00:04:56.838
Jesus Christ!
If you can't get your guys there,

00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:58.631
get SO15 on the ground now.

00:04:58.715 --> 00:05:00.216
We got something behind immigration?

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.259
Excuse me.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.386
Hey! Hey!

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.347
-How long?
-Three minutes.

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:07.598
He's through.

00:05:13.604 --> 00:05:15.314
There.
He's headed to baggage reclaim.

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:17.608
Stay on him. I need eyes
at the end of that concourse.

00:05:17.692 --> 00:05:19.527
-Yep. Coming up now.
-Head to the carousel.

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:25.700
He's headed to baggage reclaim.

00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:27.410
Give me cameras
at the end of baggage reclaim.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.911
I want eyes there.

00:05:41.632 --> 00:05:43.176
Not a Dog in sight.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:44.343
Duffy, those are your guys?

00:05:44.427 --> 00:05:45.928
No. No, ma'am. They're en route.

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.056
Duffy, surely we've got
transport police on that concourse.

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:49.891
Waiting. Inbound, two minutes.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.854
Thank you!

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.025
He's not waiting for luggage.

00:05:59.108 --> 00:06:01.069
What? He's walking straight out.

00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:12.955
Get out of the way! Move!

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.248
Move, move, move, move!

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.503
Sorry.

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.172
I'm service, I'm service.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.591
I'm service! Move now!

00:06:27.011 --> 00:06:30.181
-I need an image. Why is it dark in there?
-There's no cameras in there, ma'am.

00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:31.891
-I want eyes now!
-Confirm with Stansted.

00:06:31.974 --> 00:06:34.644
Dogs, intercept!
Suspect's now landside. Where are you?

00:06:40.691 --> 00:06:41.651
-There.
-He swapped backpacks.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.652
That's the handover.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.403
Smash the glass.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.533
This is an emergency. Please evacuate.

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:54.872
Ladies and gentlemen,
please evacuate the terminal!

00:06:54.956 --> 00:06:56.541
Evacuate the terminal all the way…

00:06:56.624 --> 00:06:58.709
-…this exit. This exit.
-Work out the safe areas.

00:06:58.793 --> 00:07:00.211
Keep them safe. Don't let anyone pass.

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:11.639
This way please. Ladies and gentlemen,
this way. Quick as you can.

00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:20.565
Move, move, move, move!

00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:24.360
Move!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.288
Move! Aside!

00:07:35.872 --> 00:07:37.915
Move! Out of the way! Now!

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.419
He's headed for the Stansted Express.

00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:45.006
Get out of the way!

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:49.760
Move! Get to the side.

00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:51.012
Come on!

00:07:53.681 --> 00:07:55.141
Get it cleared. Full evacuation.

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:56.809
Evacuate the entire train station.

00:07:56.893 --> 00:07:59.187
I want any trains
coming into Stansted halted.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:01.355
Any trains that are inbound imminently,
I need to know about it.

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:02.857
Move, move, move!

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:10.531
Move, move, move!

00:08:13.201 --> 00:08:14.493
Move, move, move!

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:17.705
-Move, move, move, move, move!
-This way!

00:08:18.748 --> 00:08:20.499
Keep moving, guys. Come on.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.753
Place is closed! Stop! Stop!

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:24.879
What are you doing?

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:43.231
Stop! No! Step away now!
Step away! Don't do it!

00:11:41.492 --> 00:11:42.493
No?

00:11:43.285 --> 00:11:44.578
Yeah? Great!

00:12:02.096 --> 00:12:03.389
Standish.

00:12:14.358 --> 00:12:16.986
-Are you all in?
-All except River and Sid.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.947
Yeah, well,
the last one in can clean my lav.

00:12:23.284 --> 00:12:25.911
I thought spooks were
supposed to be stealthy.

00:12:30.499 --> 00:12:33.836
Another day dawns on MI-Fucking Useless.

00:13:09.371 --> 00:13:10.706
Morning, Max.

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:12.750
The usual, Mr. Hobden?

00:13:12.833 --> 00:13:14.835
Yes, Max. The usual.

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:23.219
His name isn't Max.

00:13:24.512 --> 00:13:26.430
Well, it says "Max"
on the front of the shop.

00:13:26.514 --> 00:13:29.808
Yeah, but I heard the staff
call him Theo, short for Theodosios.

00:13:30.851 --> 00:13:32.520
I'll stick with "Max." Shorter.

00:13:36.732 --> 00:13:38.025
There you go.

00:13:38.108 --> 00:13:39.944
Thank you, Max.

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:02.925
What are you looking for?

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.054
A reason not to blow my brains out.

00:14:10.474 --> 00:14:12.393
He hasn't told me yet
what I'm looking for.

00:14:12.476 --> 00:14:14.562
Dumping the rubbish this side of the room.

00:14:14.645 --> 00:14:17.022
Do you think Sid will find this
as amusing as you do?

00:14:24.196 --> 00:14:25.573
-Hello, Catherine.
-Morning.

00:14:25.656 --> 00:14:26.657
Morning.

00:14:28.951 --> 00:14:31.495
Bradford driving license applications,

00:14:31.579 --> 00:14:35.249
addresses, council tax records.
Cross-check.

00:14:35.791 --> 00:14:37.293
Well, these are from 2005.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.713
The lending list
from Luton libraries in the last year.

00:14:40.796 --> 00:14:42.172
At least yours is topical.

00:14:42.256 --> 00:14:44.425
Flag any borrowing
that suggests money laundering.

00:14:44.508 --> 00:14:47.094
Really?
Someone looking that up in the library

00:14:47.177 --> 00:14:49.096
probably doesn't have
that much money to launder.

00:14:49.179 --> 00:14:51.307
Parking tickets from the Euston area.

00:14:54.059 --> 00:14:55.519
From the '90s?

00:14:55.603 --> 00:14:57.062
No stone unturned, eh?

00:14:57.146 --> 00:14:58.188
Oh, Catherine!

00:14:58.272 --> 00:15:01.275
Catherine, before you go,
these two stick-in-the-muds

00:15:01.358 --> 00:15:04.403
are giving my idea of a pub quiz team
a big thumbs down.

00:15:04.486 --> 00:15:06.238
Actually, I gave it a fat middle finger.

00:15:06.322 --> 00:15:09.867
Come on, guys! What about team spirit?
Catherine?

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:10.951
No.

00:15:11.035 --> 00:15:14.246
-"No," as in "Ask me later," or no--
-As in, "no."

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.084
Tough nut to crack, that Catherine,
but I'll get there.

00:15:19.168 --> 00:15:21.629
-Forget it. She never lightens up.
-Would you?

00:15:21.712 --> 00:15:23.881
If I was Lamb's lackey, no.

00:15:23.964 --> 00:15:26.967
No, I meant what happened before.
Before she came here.

00:15:27.051 --> 00:15:29.386
Yeah, well, I wish Lamb
would go that way.

00:15:34.308 --> 00:15:37.603
Is today the day you finally give me
something remotely challenging?

00:15:38.312 --> 00:15:41.357
Flight inquiries to Syria
from the previous decade.

00:15:41.899 --> 00:15:43.734
No, it isn't.

00:15:43.817 --> 00:15:45.402
Well, I'll set up an algorithm for that

00:15:45.486 --> 00:15:48.572
and treat the remaining nine hours
of the day as my own time.

00:15:49.698 --> 00:15:52.242
Jed? Transport police are asking

00:15:52.326 --> 00:15:55.120
if you can stop scaring people away
from that bus stop.

00:15:55.996 --> 00:15:59.291
-They could be watching us.
-Or they could be waiting for a bus.

00:16:00.042 --> 00:16:02.294
Also, Lamb says there's a new hire

00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:04.171
-at the Chinese down--
-Oh, fuck me!

00:16:04.254 --> 00:16:05.798
-And he'd like--
-I know, I know.

00:16:05.881 --> 00:16:07.132
Interview and background.

00:16:07.216 --> 00:16:10.636
And if he happens to be undocumented, it's
five free meals to look the other way.

00:16:10.719 --> 00:16:11.929
Man.

00:16:12.763 --> 00:16:15.307
No, I've been keeping me eyes
on the water.

00:16:15.391 --> 00:16:17.017
I'm just waiting for a fin to surface,

00:16:17.101 --> 00:16:22.147
but I need you to guarantee me
2,000 words once it breaks.

00:16:22.231 --> 00:16:23.982
It's like your Watergate.

00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:27.945
You know what?
I can't tell you now because it--

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:39.998
Sorry, the reason I interrupted before

00:16:40.082 --> 00:16:44.253
is because I spent a year studying
in Greece and the name caught my ear.

00:16:44.753 --> 00:16:46.922
Was a great country
a couple of thousand years ago.

00:16:47.005 --> 00:16:48.674
Yeah.

00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:52.219
And I'm interrupting now because
I was hoping I could borrow your Times.

00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:57.850
-Fine.
-Thank you.

00:16:58.684 --> 00:16:59.810
Oh, what--

00:16:59.893 --> 00:17:01.520
-Oh, my God. I am so--
-Oh, shit.

00:17:01.603 --> 00:17:03.689
-I am so sorry. I'm so sorry. Sorry.
-Oh, shit.

00:17:04.356 --> 00:17:08.736
Can I please have some towels? Okay.
Can I just have some serviettes?

00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:10.904
No, I need more serviettes.

00:17:10.988 --> 00:17:13.490
-God, I'm so--
-Here. Here.

00:17:13.574 --> 00:17:15.200
Yeah, napkins. Can we get some more?

00:17:15.284 --> 00:17:16.410
Thank you.

00:17:16.493 --> 00:17:19.997
Max, this is not enough. Have you--
Have you got any more serviettes?

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.291
-Max, pass me that.
-Take this. Take this.

00:17:23.417 --> 00:17:26.462
-Just leave it. Excuse me.
-I'm so, so clumsy.

00:17:26.545 --> 00:17:29.089
-Would you leave it?
-No, I feel so bad. Is your laptop okay?

00:17:29.173 --> 00:17:31.133
It's okay. Let me clean it up now.

00:17:31.675 --> 00:17:32.718
Fuck!

00:17:34.011 --> 00:17:35.012
Fucking…

00:17:52.404 --> 00:17:53.530
You thumped?

00:17:55.157 --> 00:17:56.366
Did you find anything?

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.328
I don't know what I'm looking for.

00:17:59.411 --> 00:18:03.499
Yeah, the remnants
of a once-promising career.

00:18:05.667 --> 00:18:09.171
Are we actually acting on any intel,
or are we just fishing?

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:11.548
Yeah, but now,
you don't get to ask questions.

00:18:12.049 --> 00:18:15.010
That's for spies who haven't shat the bed.

00:18:16.678 --> 00:18:19.139
So, what did you find? Any old notebooks?

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:22.851
The cardboard backing of one,
but no pages.

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.311
Evidence of drug use?

00:18:24.394 --> 00:18:26.355
Empty box of paracetamol, yeah.

00:18:26.438 --> 00:18:27.898
Empty booze bottles?

00:18:27.981 --> 00:18:30.150
In his recycling bin, I imagine.

00:18:30.234 --> 00:18:32.152
Oh, Christ.

00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:36.448
Is it me, or did all the fun
go out of everything around 1979?

00:18:36.532 --> 00:18:37.950
Are we looking for something,

00:18:38.033 --> 00:18:40.077
or are we just wanting him to know
that we are looking at him?

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.330
What's all this "we"? There is no "we."

00:18:43.413 --> 00:18:46.208
There's just me telling you what to do.

00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:49.294
Okay. Do you want to tell me
to put him under surveillance?

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.171
Who?

00:18:52.339 --> 00:18:53.340
Hobden.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.052
You would be doing the surveillance?

00:18:57.135 --> 00:18:58.262
Yeah.

00:18:58.929 --> 00:19:00.180
-You?
-Yeah.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.100
Well--

00:19:03.183 --> 00:19:05.769
That's a-- Well,
that's an interesting proposition,

00:19:05.853 --> 00:19:09.731
considering the last time
you were given any sort of responsibility,

00:19:09.815 --> 00:19:12.025
a load of innocent people
got blown to bits.

00:19:12.109 --> 00:19:13.277
And there it is.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.029
Well, I'm sorry you find it so tiresome,
Cartwright,

00:19:16.113 --> 00:19:19.199
but it's not the social faux pas
you seem to think it was.

00:19:19.283 --> 00:19:22.995
You didn't break wind
during someone's wedding vows.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:27.749
What was it? 149 dead, 212 injured,

00:19:28.542 --> 00:19:31.795
Three million in damages,
half a billion in lost revenue--

00:19:31.879 --> 00:19:33.463
It was a training exercise.

00:19:33.547 --> 00:19:38.093
If a pilot crashes a simulator,
he doesn't then brush it off and go,

00:19:38.176 --> 00:19:40.637
"Well, I'm sorry.
It was a fucking exercise,"

00:19:40.721 --> 00:19:43.974
and then expect to be
put behind the wheel of a 747.

00:19:44.057 --> 00:19:47.227
-It's not the same thing.
-No, it's worse, you tit.

00:19:50.063 --> 00:19:52.816
-You're gonna do this every day then?
-If I didn't hate the sight of you,

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:55.611
I'd come to your home
and do it at the weekends too.

00:19:56.653 --> 00:20:00.782
I am surrounded by fuckups
in this building,

00:20:00.866 --> 00:20:02.910
but you are the gold standard of fuckups.

00:20:02.993 --> 00:20:05.370
By all rights, you shouldn't even be here.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.749
You should've skipped this purgatory
and gone straight to hell.

00:20:08.832 --> 00:20:10.042
Melted you down for glue.

00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:13.921
But you avoided that
because your name is Cartwright.

00:20:14.004 --> 00:20:17.424
So when you wonder why I have you
going through the rubbish

00:20:17.507 --> 00:20:20.719
of a disgraced right-wing journo,
wonder no more.

00:20:23.263 --> 00:20:24.973
It's because I don't like you.

00:20:26.099 --> 00:20:27.559
And I want you to quit.

